"Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released 'Workflows', an orchestration layer to ensure stability and visibility of enterprise AI processes. Workflows helps companies reliably transition their AI processes from proof-of-concept to production environments. Solve chronic problems in enterprise AI environments, such as silent errors in the pipeline, network timeouts, and insufficient human approval processes. Workflows can be defined in Python, managed in Studio, and executed by anyone in the organization through Le Chat. Speaking of Voxtral Mistral AI has launched 'Voxtral TTS', a 4B parameter lightweight TTS model that supports 9 languages ​​and is optimized for emotional expression and natural speech. Lightweight model with 4B parameters, highly scalable and cost-effective, with ultra-low latency Supports 9 languages ​​and various dialects, including English, French, German, Spanish, Dutch, Portuguese, Italian, Hindi, and Arabic As a result of human evaluation, it showed higher naturalness compared to ElevenLabs Flash v2.5 and provided the same quality as ElevenLabs v3. Introducing Forge Mistral AI has launched 'Forge', a system that allows companies to directly learn specialized AI models based on unique internal data and knowledge. Domain-specific AI models can be built using internal data such as engineering standards, policies, and code bases held by a company. Developing models optimized for complex system operation through partnerships with major global companies such as ASML and Ericsson. Supports pre-learning, post-learning, and reinforcement learning to develop sophisticated AI agents that meet the company's internal policies and operational purposes. Introducing Mistral Small 4 Mistral AI has launched Mistral Small 4, a new model that combines inference, multimodal, and agent coding capabilities into a single model. By integrating inference, multimodal, and agent-based coding functions into one, we reduce the complexity of model selection and maximize versatility. Distributed under the Apache 2.0 license, it contributes to the open source ecosystem and provides high accessibility and customization. It supports 128 expert (MoE) structures and 256k context windows, enabling efficient scaling and long text processing. The reasoning_effort parameter allows you to dynamically adjust the model's reasoning speed and depth depending on the complexity of the task. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI will participate as a founding member of NVIDIA's 'Nemotron Coalition' to jointly develop open, cutting-edge AI models and promote ecosystem expansion. Mistral AI joins the NVIDIA-led ‘Nemotron Coalition’ as a founding member to accelerate the development of open, cutting-edge AI models. We combine NVIDIA's computing resources and technology with Mistral AI's architecture and training technology to promote efficient AI model development. Announces new ‘Mistral Small 4’ model to support open model ecosystem and strengthens efforts to democratize AI. NVIDIA, KRAFTON, NC and Reigning ‘League of Legends’ Champions T1 Celebrate RTX Spark at Korea’s PC Bangs NVIDIA has unveiled its new superchip 'RTX Spark', designed for the era of personal AI agents, to the Korean gaming market. NVIDIA collaborates with major Korean gaming companies such as KRAFTON and NC to support a high-performance gaming environment on RTX Spark-based systems. CEO Jensen Huang visited a major PC room in Seoul and demonstrated RTX Spark and new game technologies using it (PUBG Ally, etc.) together with T1, KRAFTON, and NC. RTX Spark supports DLSS 4.5, ray tracing, and more, and can run AAA games on thin laptops and low-power desktops. China wants slimmer EVs after batteries and features made them too heavy for parking spaces The Chinese government is strengthening regulations on electric vehicles that are too heavy and large due to large batteries and excessive features and is forcing improvements in energy efficiency. The average weight of electric vehicles in China has increased by one-third compared to 2012, causing a parking space shortage problem. Large batteries and the installation of various additional functions in the vehicle were identified as the main cause of the increase in vehicle weight. From January 1, 2026, the Chinese government will implement the world's first mandatory energy consumption standards for electric vehicles, mandating vehicle efficiency. UK plans to buy AI chips from British firms to stop them leaving for the US The British government is pursuing a strategy of directly purchasing products from domestic AI chip companies in order to prevent them from leaking overseas and foster the industry. The British government plans to protect the domestic technology ecosystem through a 'strategic purchasing' plan to purchase chips directly from domestic semiconductor companies. This plan aims to foster the AI ​​hardware industry to achieve 5% global semiconductor market share and £37 billion in sales. We aim to prevent overseas sales of major companies such as ARM and Graphcore and provide a stable source of demand domestically. Trump signs memo putting ‘most advanced AI’ into military hands and banning vendors from pulling the plug President Donald Trump signed the National Security Presidential Memorandum (NSPM-11) to accelerate the adoption of cutting-edge AI by the U.S. military and intelligence community and prevent vendors from arbitrarily discontinuing military AI without government approval. We established a framework to accelerate the adoption of cutting-edge AI models by the U.S. military and intelligence community. AI vendors will no longer be able to disable, degrade, or modify military-dependent AI systems without government approval. Directs the Secretary of Defense to revise the Autonomous Weapon Systems Operations Directive (DoD Directive 3000.09) within 90 days. OpenAI adds Lockdown Mode to ChatGPT to block data theft from prompt injection attacks OpenAI has introduced 'Lockdown Mode' in ChatGPT to prevent data theft through prompt injection attacks. Lockdown Mode disables features with potential data leaks, including live web browsing, agent mode, and deep research. This feature is available to users of all ChatGPT plans: Free, Go, Plus, Pro, and ChatGPT Business. Although it blocks the path through which an attacker can steal data externally, it does not prevent the injection attack itself from occurring. Best 21 Low-Code and No-Code AI Tools in 2026 Introducing 21 AI-based low-code and no-code tools that will enable application development by 2026 with just text prompts. Low-code and no-code platforms have evolved beyond drag-and-drop methods to an environment where AI automatically creates applications and agents. We help non-developers, startups, and small teams quickly build ready-to-use products without a separate development team. A variety of tools, including Atoms, Bubble, Adalo, and Glide, automate the process from web, mobile, and backend configuration to deployment. Meet Harness-1: A 20B Retrieval Subagent Trained With Reinforcement Learning Inside a Stateful Search Harness on gpt-oss-20b This is an introduction to the 20B-scale search subagent 'Harness-1', which improves search efficiency by separating search decisions and record management. Harness-1 reduces complexity by allowing the search agent to focus only on search decisions and having the external 'Stateful Harness' take charge of state management. To solve the problem of existing search agents performing search decisions and routine bookkeeping simultaneously, we adopted a 'stateful cognitive offloading' method. Harness-1 was trained through reinforcement learning based on gpt-oss-20b, and the harness code and model weights were released. NVIDIA garak Tutorial: Build a Complete Defensive LLM Red-Teaming Workflow with Custom Probes and Detectors This tutorial explains how to build a red team workflow using NVIDIA garak, an LLM security testing framework. Step-by-step guide to building an LLM red team and security testing workflow using NVIDIA garak Includes how to explore plugins, run model scans, analyze results, and create custom probes/detectors. Real hugging face model scanning and programmatic multi-probe evaluation practice Sponsors especially OPENAI CODEX voucher usage for codex - openAI challange Hackathon participants ask questions about how to use OpenAI Codex vouchers and share registration issues. I am having difficulty because I do not know where to enter the OpenAI Codex voucher. There was an initial registration error with the Modal voucher, but it was successfully resolved on the second attempt. The winning team of the hackathon will receive $10,000 in prize money and a ChatGPT Pro subscription. Pokemon Emerald ported to WebAssembly (100k FPS) Community discussion about a project that recompiled the 2004 game Pokemon Emerald into WebAssembly (WASM) to run it in the browser. Pokémon Emerald, reverse-engineered by the Pret team, was recompiled with WASM and run in a web browser. Community users are reporting issues such as menu crashes and display bugs, and the developer has revealed plans to fix them. The save feature works, and there is ongoing improvement and experimentation, with some users creating audio-enabled forks. If LLM has human-like attributes, so does Age of Empires II When assessing anthropomorphism in LLM, we point out the problems with the approach that assumes the human-like properties of the model and discuss that interpretation may vary depending on the substrate. In LLM research, evaluation methods premised on human-like attributes may be circular or have low informativeness. The example of neural network implementation in Age of Empires II suggests that it is possible to implement an entity equivalent to LLM if the substrate is sufficiently strong. Explicit measurement standards are needed for empirical discussion, and an approach that assumes LLM non-uniqueness is needed rather than assuming that anthropomorphic properties are independent of temperament. Ask HN: Why are HN users so opposed to AI? We discuss the pros and cons of AI technology and the diverse perspectives of developers within the Hacker News community. Concerns are raised about the low quality of code written by AI and the incurring of technical debt. Some developers leverage AI as a productivity tool that speeds up product development and deployment by 10x. Positions on AI within the community vary depending on how questions are asked in posts, individual work philosophies, and expectations of tools. S&amp;P 500 rejects SpaceX and blocks inclusion of OpenAI and Anthropic S&P Dow Jones Indices' decision to maintain S&P 500 index inclusion criteria has blocked the possibility of early inclusion for SpaceX, OpenAI, and Anthropic. S&P Dow Jones Indices has decided not to change its existing S&P 500 inclusion criteria, including the financial viability test, 12-month waiting period, and minimum public equity requirements. This decision precludes early inclusion in the S&P 500 for large tech companies like SpaceX, OpenAI, and Anthropic that are unprofitable or have low public equity ratios. If the existing criteria had been changed, SpaceX could have expected passive fund purchase inflows of $14 billion, OpenAI by $8 billion, and Anthropic by $4.6 billion. Nvidia proposes a monster CPU system for Windows PCs Analyzing the features and value of a high-performance CPU/GPU integrated system based on 128GB integrated memory and 6,144 CUDA cores proposed by Nvidia for Windows PC. Optimized for local AI model execution by adopting a unified architecture where the CPU and GPU use 128GB of shared memory as a single pool. It is equipped with a Cortex-X925-based CPU and up to 6,144 CUDA cores, but is designed to focus on local AI workloads rather than existing high-performance games. There are advantages of local AI execution, such as data security, cost reduction, and zero-copy operation, but there are also technical limitations such as memory replacement and bandwidth limitations. ML reading group to read recent interesting and trending papers from ICML/ICLR/NeurIPS [D] We are recruiting a weekend reading group for PhD students to discuss their latest papers on the topic of interpretability and robustness in machine learning. Research papers in the areas of interpretability and robustness are covered in depth. Read and discuss recent trend papers presented at major conferences such as ICML, ICLR, and NeurIPS. We are recruiting participants from interested doctoral students and machine learning researchers. Research collection of Arxiv whitepapers [R] This is an example of organizing approximately 1,700 archive (Arxiv) papers collected after the launch of ChatGPT into 90 categories and sharing them by constructing a web-based 'Inquiring Lines'. We collected approximately 1,700 Arxiv papers and related research excerpts accumulated since the launch of ChatGPT. The collected papers were classified into more than 90 thematic categories, and a cross-reference system was established using wiki links. A web project called 'Inquiring Lines' published 6000 research summary lines and prompts to explore related research. AI on an older PC with a CPU that apparently doesn't have AVX >:,( This is asking for advice on the difficulties experienced by users who want to use an old PC as an AI server due to the CPU's lack of AVX instruction set support. A user wants to install a high-performance GPU (2 Nvidia 1080ti) on an old PC and use it as an AI server. An obstacle is the older QX6700 CPU, which does not support the Advanced Vector Extensions (AVX) instruction set required to run most LLMs. We asked the community if it was possible to run AI by overcoming CPU limitations and if there were other solutions. Roguelite MMO Beta Vibe Coded In 4 Weeks A 10-year senior developer leveraged AI to develop a browser-based Roguelite MMO game in 4 weeks. Using an AI coding assistant, the development period, which previously took more than a year, was shortened to 4 weeks. The browser-based Roguelite MMO is currently in beta. The latest update adds new game content such as casino, horse racing, and fishing. I got tired of Al making stuff up about my PDFs, so I built something that actually cites its sources We developed and released a question-and-answer tool that prevents users from experiencing problems with PDF documents being hallucinated by existing AI and clearly presents sources of evidence. To solve the problem of existing AI distorting or hallucinating document content, we developed a tool that cites evidence based on files. You can ask questions by uploading files in various formats such as PDF, Word, CSV, and images, and the exact page on which the answer is based will be displayed. It provides a variety of functions for learning and practice, including web search functions, document summarization, automatic flashcard generation, and resume review. Best AI PowerPoint maker for people who already have content? Rather than creating a presentation from a topic, the goal is to find an AI tool that converts large amounts of existing material into highly readable slides. Existing AI presentation creation tools are mainly focused on generating content based on specific topics. Users need a tool that can convert already organized materials such as notes, meeting transcripts, and documents into neat slides. The goal is to find the optimal AI service that reorganizes text-rich original data into readable slides. this just isn't sustainable. This is in response to the criticism that the inference cost of current AI models is very high and therefore economically unsustainable. The actual computing costs incurred when using high-performance AI models for simple data summarization tasks are very high. Even with subsidies, service costs are still high and there is a large gap with actual infrastructure operating costs. Concerns that it is difficult to secure long-term sustainability with the current AI model operating cost structure. llama.cpp Gemma4 MTP support merged! Support for the Gemma4 MTP model structure has been merged into the llama.cpp open source project. Added latest model support to llama.cpp library Secure official compatibility for Gemma4 MTP architecture You don't need a GPU to run gemma-4-26B-A4B An example showing that the latest large language model (LLM) can be run smoothly without a GPU even in a low-end CPU environment. Successfully ran the 'gemma-4-26B-A4B' model without GPU on a low-end computer with an i5-8500 CPU and 32GB RAM. Can be run at a speed of approximately 7 tokens per second using the Koboldcpp tool in a Linux environment. It is emphasized that expensive GPU equipment is not necessarily required to run the latest LLM. Qwen 3.6 27B KV cache quant benchmarks: 75 pairs, q8/q6/q5/q4, KVarN, Turbo/TCQ We cover benchmark results for different KV cache quantization schemes for the Qwen 3.6 27B model. Various KV cache quantization techniques such as KVarN, q8/q6/q5/q4, TurboQuant, and TCQ were tested on the Qwen 3.6 27B model. Uses BeeLlama.cpp (a fork of llama.cpp) as the inference engine to support various quantization types. Detailed benchmark results and in-depth analysis are provided through related articles. What’s your most unusual non-LLM AI you actually use daily? Community recommendations and discussions about unique or undervalued non-LLM AI tools that we use every day. We share unique or undervalued non-LLM-based AI tools that users use in their daily lives. Collect little-known or niche AI ​​use cases. Discusses the use of special-purpose AI technologies beyond LLM. Clustering 3x Jetson Nano Orin Supers This article introduces a project to build a cluster for distributed AI learning and inference using three Jetson Nano Orin Supers. Following Raspberry Pi and Mac mini, we are publishing a series of guides to building a distributed computing cluster with Jetson Nano Orin Super. The goal is to help users easily access distributed AI model training and inference using their own hardware. After completing hardware setup and network configuration, we will continue with practice using smolcluster. How LLMs Actually Work This is a guide that explains the core mechanisms of the Transformer architecture, which is the basis of modern large-scale language models (LLM), without mathematical complexity and in an easy-to-understand manner. LLM mainly shares a structure of stacked transformer blocks and operates through key elements such as tokenization, embedding, position encoding, and attention. The model does not read the text directly, but processes the data using integer IDs (token IDs) converted through a tokenization process. For efficiency, tokenization is performed on a subword basis rather than entire words, which is advantageous for processing new or rare words. What e-reader tablets do published authors use? My survey found results beyond the Kindle This is a survey of published authors to find out which e-reader they prefer other than Amazon Kindle. Research on which e-readers authors prefer for reading and annotating. Amazon Kindle remains the most popular device due to its easy-to-use interface and extensive library of books. The article introduces the Kindle Paperwhite, which features a 7-inch display and waterproof design, as a recommended model. The feature Apple needs to make HomePod stand out isn't audio-related This emphasizes that for Apple's HomePod to differentiate itself in the market, upgrading Siri's generative AI is more important than audio quality. HomePod's biggest competitive edge is Siri, and Siri's generative AI upgrade is expected at the upcoming WWDC. Improved Siri can greatly improve your music listening experience, including music recommendations and playlist creation. Siri must be linked with Apple's ecosystem data (calendar, notifications, contacts, etc.) to support daily work management and customized services (recipe provision, route navigation, etc.). I saw the Surface Laptop Ultra at Computex and it's clear: Microsoft has gone beastmode This article analyzes the specifications and features of the high-performance AI laptop 'Surface Laptop Ultra' announced by Microsoft at Computex 2026. Equipped with Nvidia's new RTX Spark SoC (20-core CPU, GeForce RTX 5070-class GPU, and up to 128GB integrated memory), powerful AI tasks and creative performance Equipped with 15-inch mini-LED PixelSense Ultra touchscreen, supporting brightness of up to 2000 nits Premium high-performance laptop designed for developers, professional creators, and AI power users Android Auto is way more customizable than you might realize - 6 tricks to try ASAP An article introducing six useful setup methods that allow users to tailor Android Auto's interface, notifications, and app configuration to suit their needs. You can increase convenience by deleting unused apps from Android Auto's app list and arranging them in the order you want them. You can personalize your display by locking the day/night mode or adjusting it to sync according to your smartphone settings. Routines and shortcuts allow you to perform multiple tasks at once, including making calls, controlling your smart home, and executing Gemini commands. Years of emergency prep taught me how to storm-proof my solar generators We'll cover how to safely and efficiently maintain your portable solar generator for emergencies and prepare for storms. Solar generators are a useful source of power in an emergency, but they can also be a hazard if not properly prepared. As extreme weather events become more frequent, the use of solar power generators is increasing to secure emergency power at home. Based on years of experience and survival skills training, we emphasize the preparation process to optimize solar power generators for disaster situations. ExtendDB: Open Source Amazon DynamoDB Compatible Adapter with Pluggable Storage Backends ExtendDB, an open source project released by AWS, is an adapter that is compatible with the Amazon DynamoDB API and supports various storage backends such as PostgreSQL. Existing AWS SDKs and tools can be used without modification, increasing the flexibility of the execution environment for DynamoDB workloads. It runs as a single binary written in Rust, and its pluggable design allows you to add storage backends other than PostgreSQL. It can be used to operate DynamoDB-compatible workloads in local development, CI testing, and on-premises environments. “Chat is dead”...ChatGPT, ‘Agent Super App’ countdown to revamp Open AI completely reorganizes ChatGPT from a passive chatbot to an 'agent super app' that automatically performs tasks by linking with external apps. OpenAI plans to carry out the largest overhaul since the launch of ChatGPT in stages in the coming weeks. When the user gives instructions in natural language, the AI ​​understands the intention and switches to directly running an external app from a partner company to complete the task. This reorganization is a strategy to eliminate low-profit services ahead of the IPO and transform into an agent- and coding-centered platform that can maximize sales. Kim Hyeong-jun, CEO of Squeeze Beats, “Expanding beyond lightweight AI to a ‘physical AI’ solution” Squeeze Beats expands its business into physical AI and robot learning data construction solutions by optimizing World Foundation model inference based on AI lightweight technology. Squeeze Beats is expanding its business area to solutions that support the construction of physical AI and robot data by focusing on its existing AI lightweight technology capabilities. The core service, 'Yetter', realizes optimal performance on various hardware, including running the NVIDIA 'Cosmos 3-Nano' model 3.3 times faster. The new solution 'RoBoost' triples the inference speed of the world model, reduces computational costs by one-third, and increases the rate of securing high-quality datasets from 15% to 50%. OpenAI unveils ‘lockdown mode’ that prevents prompt injection... “Restricts external connections” OpenAI has unveiled a 'lockdown mode' that restricts external network connections to prevent sensitive information leaks due to prompt injection attacks. OpenAI launched 'Lockdown Mode' to reduce the risk of data leakage in response to prompt injection attacks. This mode enhances security by restricting functions that connect to external networks, such as real-time web browsing, deep research, and agent mode. It is intended for individuals and organizations that handle sensitive data and can be activated in the Security menu of your account settings. Masayoshi Son \"Next-generation AI is designed by AI, not humans... Superintelligence will arrive within two years.\" Softbank Chairman Masayoshi Son predicted that the advent of superintelligence (ASI) will be brought forward within two years due to the phenomenon of recursive self-improvement (RSI), in which AI designs its own next-generation models. The pace of technological development is accelerating exponentially as AI designs its own next-generation models. Major companies such as OpenAI, Antropic, and Google are already introducing recursive self-improvement (RSI), which uses AI for model development. Chairman Son believes that the AI ​​revolution is 50 times larger than the dot-com revolution and that it is a good time to invest despite the bubble theory. LGU+ “AIDC 5 trillion won contract in 2030… Presenting AI infrastructure standards” LG U+ announced its next-generation AI infrastructure strategy centered on the Paju AI Data Center and set a goal of achieving 5 trillion won in cumulative contracts by 2030. We plan to propose next-generation AI infrastructure standards and strengthen domestic competitiveness by leveraging the synergy of 'One LG', a technological collaboration with LG affiliates. Beyond providing data center facilities, we aim to become an 'AI Factory Operator' that integrates GPU management, power, and cooling. We aim to achieve 5 trillion won in cumulative contracts by 2030 and grow 15-20% in average annual sales, and the contract for Building 1 of the Paju AI Data Center has already been completed. Joo-pyeong Lee, Executive Director of Samsung SDS, “Manufacturing AI core data is time series” Samsung SDS Executive Director Joo-pyeong Lee emphasized the importance of securing high-quality time series manufacturing data and building a dedicated infrastructure to succeed in the AI ​​transformation (M.AX) of the manufacturing industry. For successful manufacturing AI, securing economies of scale through sharing and utilizing large-scale manufacturing data is key. Unlike text-oriented LLM data, manufacturing AI data is mainly time series data from sensors and industrial equipment. AI data centers, which are manufacturing AI infrastructure, must be designed in the form of a supercomputer with thousands of GPUs connected through a high-speed network. Manufacturing data is difficult to learn due to the difficulty in masking sensitive information, its massive scale, and the difficulty in obtaining the correct answer. In an era where AI creates AI, where is the direction of developers? As AI is deeply involved in the entire software development process, the role of developers is changing from coding to architecture design, result verification, and control. Major AI companies such as OpenAI and Antropic are introducing AI agents that perform everything from code writing to testing into actual development sites. Unlike coding assistants of the past, modern AI analyzes and modifies entire code bases on its own and performs repetitive tasks autonomously. The core competencies of developers are moving from simply writing a lot of code to defining problems, designing systems, and managing and taking responsibility for the quality and security of AI output."